(a) the number of countries and foreign nationals who have benefited under the Indian Technical and Economic Cooperation (ITEC) programme during 2024-25 and 2025-26;
(b) the budgetary allocations made and expenditure incurred under the programme during the said period;
(c) the number of new training courses or institutions added under ITEC recently; and
(d) whether Government proposes to expand ITEC’s reach to any new partner countries and if so, the details, thereof?

(a) whether Government has conducted any review of the implementation of''Ek Ped Maa Ke Naam'' campaign;
(b) if so, the details thereof;
(c) the details of measures taken to strengthen public participation, institutional support and community involvement under the campaign;
(d) whether any mechanism has been established for digital monitoring, survival assessment and long-term maintenance of plantations carried out through the campaign; and
(e) if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether the Multi-Model Ensemble forecasting system adopted by the India Meteorological Department has improved the accuracy and reliability of long-range monsoon forecasts;
(b) if so, the details thereof;
(c) the steps being taken to address challenges such as the spring predictability barrier in long-range monsoon prediction;
(d) whether any new modelling and observational systems are being introduced to improve prediction of extreme rainfall events in hilly and coastal regions; and
(e) if so, the details thereof, and the roadmap for further strengthening India’s long-range forecasting capabilities in the coming years?

(a) whether Government has taken any measures to strengthen digital access to India's cultural heritage through the 'Unnat Bharat Sanskriti Portal'(Advanced Indian Culture Portal);
(b) the details of initiatives undertaken to improve accessibility, multilingual availability and user engagement on the portal through advanced digital technologies;
(c) whether any mechanism has been established to facilitate the unification of museums, libraries, archives and other cultural institutions with the portal for expansion of digital cultural resources;
(d) if so, the details thereof; and
(e) the manner in which the portal is expected to promote broader public access to India's cultural heritage and support research and preservation?

(a) the details of achievements of Sanchar Saathi portal and mobile application in preventing telecom-related fraud since its launch;
(b) whether any institutional mechanism exists for coordination between DoT, banks and law enforcement agencies through the Digital Intelligence Platform to act on fraud reports in real time;
(c) the steps being taken to ensure accessibility of Sanchar Saathi services across regional languages and among first-time mobile users;
(d) if so, whether any measures have been taken to mandate availability of Sanchar Saathi app on mobile devices sold in India; and
(e) the future roadmap for strengthening citizen-centric telecom security tools under Sanchar Saathi?

(a) the State-wise amount sanctioned and utilised from the Nirbhaya Fund during Financial Year 2025-26;
(b) the number of One Stop Centres and Women Helplines strengthened or made functional through this Fund during the said period;
(c) the number of States where additional safety infrastructure projects have been approved under the Fund; and
(d) the additional steps being taken to expedite utilisation of the Fund for women's safety and protection schemes?

(a) whether Government has undertaken any review of decentralised skill planning through District Skill Development Plans;
(b) if so, the details thereof;
(c) the progress achieved in preparation and implementation of District Skill Development Plans across the State of Gujarat;
(d) whether any institutional mechanism has been established to align district-level skill planning with local industry demand and livelihood opportunities; and
(e) if so, the details thereof?

(a) the status of the implementation of digital toll collection initiatives on the National Highways;
(b) the information regarding measures undertaken to facilitate technology-enabled toll collection on the National Highway network;
(c) whether the Ministry is planning  to expand barrier-free electronic toll collection; and
(d) if so, the details thereof?

(a) the total number of livestock that have been registered under the 'Pashu Aadhar' 12-digit unique identification system on the Bharat Pashudhan Portal so far;
(b) the number of stakeholders provided with digital identity under the National Fisheries Digital Platform (NFDP) and the manner in which it facilitates access to credit and insurance;
(c) the number of Kisan Credit Card (KCC) applications relating to the animal husbandry and fisheries sectors approved under this digital ecosystem so far; and
(d) the steps taken to integrate Pashu Aadhar-linked health, breeding and productivity records with veterinary service delivery and disease surveillance systems across the country?

(a) the current status of Bharat Taxi, operated by Sahakar Taxi Cooperative Limited, including the number of registered drivers and customers, as on date;
(b) the cities in which the service is currently operational and the details of its proposed expansion to other cities, including the timeline for reaching 500 cities;
(c) the manner in which the driver-owned cooperative model is expected to ensure better earnings and welfare for drivers as compared to existing app-based ride-hailing platforms; and
(d) whether any regulatory or financial support has been extended by Government for the expansion of this initiative?

(a) the number of houses sanctioned, completed, and handed over to beneficiaries under the Pradhan Mantri Awas Yojana-Gramin (PMAY-G) during the financial year 2025-26, State-wise;
(b) the current status of the construction of the remaining houses and the target set for their completion; 
(c) the steps taken to ensure quality construction and timely completion as well as convergence with other schemes such as Jal Jeevan Mission, electricity and LPG connections;
(d) whether special priority has been accorded to Particularly Vulnerable Tribal Groups (PVTGs), aspirational districts, and disaster-prone areas; and
(e) if so, the details of the funds released and expenditure incurred during the last two financial years?

(a) whether community radio stations are being integrated with district-level disaster management and emergency communication plans;
(b) if so, the details thereof;
(c) whether provision has been made to provide backup power arrangements and emergency protocols for these community radio stations; and
(d) if so, the details thereof?

(a) the criteria adopted for the selection of agro-processing clusters under the Pradhan Mantri Kisan SAMPADA Yojana (PMKSY);
(b) whether priority is being accorded to the products identified under the One District One Product (ODOP) initiative at the district level for such clusters;
(c) if so, the details thereof;
(d) whether the Ministry monitors if the approved clusters are attracting the expected investment after their establishment; and
(e) if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether Government has implemented the Khelo Bharat Niti, 2025 across States and Union-Territories and if so, the details thereof;
(b) the details of measures taken to strengthen grassroots sports infrastructure, talent identification, sports science, coaching and athlete development under the Khelo Bharat Niti, including the status of Khelo India Centres across the country, Sate/UT-wise;
(c) whether Government has introduced mechanisms to encourage greater participation of private sector through Public-Private-Partnerships(PPPs), Corporate Social Responsibility(CSR), sports entrepreneurship and startups for strengthening sports ecosystem and if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the targets and outcomes envisaged under the Niti, particularly with regard to India's preparations for 2036 Olympic Games and making India a global sporting powerhouse?

(a) the number of cases taken up and disposed of through e-Lok Adalats during the last three years, State-wise and year wise;
(b) the total amount of monetary settlement arrived through e-Lok Adalats during the said period;
(c) the States/Union Territories where e-Lok Adalats have been introduced or expanded during the said period; and
(d) the further steps proposed to expand this initiative across the country?

(a) the progress made under Pradhan Mantri Kisan SAMPADA Yojana in creating modern food processing infrastructure and value addition facilities in all States including  Maharashtra;
(b) the number of projects sanctioned, completed, and the employment generated through the scheme district-wise including Maharashtra;
(c) the steps taken to reduce post-harvest losses, promote farmer producer organisations, and enhance farmer income especially in the Khandesh and Marthwada rigion of Maharashtra; and
(d) the overall impact on food processing capacity, exports and growth of the sector?

(a) the major initiatives taken by Government during the last two years to promote tourism in India, including infrastructure development and digital promotion;
(b) the progress and impact of the 'Ek Bharat Shreshtha Bharat' programme in promoting cultural tourism and people-to-people connections across States and Union Territories; and
(c) the steps taken to boost international tourist arrivals, ease of travel and development of specific tourism products like spiritual, eco, adventure and heritage tourism?

(a) whether Government has upgraded the National Career Service (NCS) portal to make it more user-friendly and accessible for job seekers and if so, the details thereof;
(b) the number of Model Career Centres (MCCs) operational in the country and their role in promoting the use of NCS portal;
(c) whether the system predicts current and future skill requirements for the youth and by when a single-window portal for job seekers would be launched; and
(d) whether the NCS portal utilises advanced technologies like Artificial Intelligence (AI) and Meta Data to effectively match job demand and supply?

(a) the number of participants recorded by MY Bharat Budget Quest 2026 in its national-level quiz this year;
(b) the details of interactions between State/UT winners and the Prime Minister held on the 15th March, 2026;
(c) whether the Ministry has expanded the MY Bharat portal registrations to include over 5 crore Indian youth;
(d) if so, the details thereof; and
(e) how the "Viksit Bharat Youth Parliament" initiative (March 2026) has influenced the latest youth-centric policy decisions of the Ministry?

(a) whether the Ministry has operationalised ?500 crore initiative for promotion of sports' goods manufacturing;
(b) if so, the details thereof;
(c) the manner in which dedicated research in material sciences under this initiative is helping to produce affordable, high-quality indigenous hockey sticks;
(d) the specific milestones achieved by Augmenting Study Materials in Indian Languages through Translation and Academic Writing (ASMITA) initiative in promoting gender neutrality in competitive sports during 2025-26; and
(e) how the Target Olympic Podium Scheme (TOPS) successfully supported the training of winter athletes for 2026 Milano Cortina?

(a) whether the Ministry has successfully launched the pilot project to train 10,000 tour guides in collaboration with IIMs;
(b) how ‘Chalo India’ Global Diaspora Campaign would convert 1 lakh free e-visas into actual tourist arrivals by 2026;
(c) the details of specific curriculum changes which are being implemented to transition the National Council for Hotel Management into a National Institute; 
(d) whether the Dekho Apna Desh People's Choice 2024 winners' ceremony held in February, 2026 has incentivised students towards tourism education; and
(e) if so, the details thereof?

(a) how the new Employees’ Provident Fund (EPF) Scheme 2026 provides a legally robust foundation for transition to the Social Security Code;
(b) the details of administrative simplifications introduced in the single SOP for EPF Exemption approved in March 2026;
(c) whether 8.25 per cent interest rate for Financial Year 2025-26 has been recommended for all subscribers;
(d) if so, the details thereof; and
(e) how the Amnesty Scheme for exempted trusts successfully resolved pending litigation to protect worker interests?

(a) the manner in which the new React-based architecture has helped in improving the scalability and search speed for 18.23 crore pages of digitized records;
(b) the specific impact of 3D walkthroughs and 360-degree virtual tours on digital engagement for students and researchers;
(c) whether the new section on 'Iconic Battles of India' on the portal has been integrated into the national history curriculum in 2026;
(d) if so, the details thereof; and
(e) the number of visitors who have accessed the 1.8 lakh digitized museum artifacts through the upgraded integrated cultural platform?

(a) whether Government has conducted any recent assessment of domestic crude oil and natural gas production in the country, if so, the details thereof, particularly in the context of India's growing dependence on energy imports;
(b) if so, the details thereof, including the production levels of crude oil and natural gas, during the last three years;
(c) whether Government has taken any steps to ensure a steady import of oil from foreign countries amidst rising war tensions in the West; and
(d) if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether Government has undertaken any review of the contribution of MSMEs to the country’s exports, particularly in view of the increasing participation of Micro, Small and Medium Enterprises (MSMEs) in global value chains;
(b) if so, the details thereof including the share of MSMEs in India’s total exports during the last three years;
(c) whether Government proposes to strengthen technology upgradation, digital adoption and quality certification support for MSMEs in order to improve their competitiveness in domestic and international markets; and
(d) if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether Government has undertaken any assessment of groundwater depletion in various parts of the country, particularly in view of increasing pressure on groundwater resources due to agricultural and domestic usage;
(b) if so, the details thereof;
(c) whether Government proposes to strengthen water conservation initiatives and aquifer recharge programmes under schemes such as Atal Bhujal Yojana and other groundwater management initiatives to ensure sustainable water availability; and
(d) if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether Government has undertaken any recent review of the implementation of Jal Jeevan Mission, particularly with regard to ensuring Functional Household Tap Connections (FHTCs) to rural households across the country, and;
(b) if so, the details thereof;
(c) whether Government has identified States or districts where the coverage of tap water connections remains below the national average and the steps being taken to accelerate the implementation of the scheme in such areas; and
(d) if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether Government has undertaken any assessment of the progress made under the Pradhan Mantri Awas Yojana–Urban (PMAY-U) towards achieving the objective of ‘Housing for All’ in urban areas, particularly with regard to the number of houses sanctioned, completed and under construction across various States;
(b) if so, the details thereof;
(c) whether Government proposes to continue or restructure the scheme beyond its present implementation period in order to address the remaining shortage of affordable housing in urban areas; and
(d) if so, the details thereof?

(a) the number of mega food parks and agro-processing clusters that have become operational in the country particularly in Bihar during the last three years;
(b) the number of processing units within these parks that have commenced production during the said period;
(c) whether the delays in milestone infrastructure or shared facilities have adversely affected the utilization of these parks including, in Bihar;
(d) if so, the details thereof;
(e) the steps being taken by Government to attract private investment in underutilized parks; and
(f) the number of employment opportunities generated so far, through these facilities particularly in Bihar?

(a) the number of pulses processing units approved up to December, 2025, under Aatmanirbharta Mission in Pulses along with the details of the units selected on priority basis in the first phase, State-wise;

(b) the phased plan and timeline for distribution of 88 lakh free seed kits of high-yielding varieties of tur and masoor, along with the number of districts identified for this initial implementation; and

(c) the extent of area that has, so far, been identified or mapped against the target of bringing an additional 35 lakh hectares under pulses cultivation?

(a) the current status of steel production capacity in the country; 
(b) the role of the National Steel Policy (NSP), 2017 in the growth of steel production in the country and the roadmap to sustain this growth until 2030; and
(c) whether the NSP, 2017 is aligned with ensuring domestic production of special steel and alloys for strategic use in defense and aerospace sectors under the Make in India program, if so, the details thereof?

(a) the total length of railway tracks in kilometers, identified for renewal across the entire rail network, including Maharashtra;
(b) the targets set for track renewal during the last four years including the year 2025-26, year-wise;
(c) the length of railway track in kilometers, that has been actually renewed during the said period across the entire rail network, including Maharashtra; and
(d) whether there is any pending work, if so, the details thereof, zone-wise, including Rajasthan?

(a)  the total number of global  Electric Vehicle (EV) manufacturers who have applied under the Scheme to Promote Manufacturing of Electric Cars(SMEC) since March 2024 till now;
(b) the number of companies out of these that have started the process of land acquisition or plant construction;
(c) the States which are emerging as major EV hubs under the said scheme; and
(d) the monitoring mechanism in place to ensure that the approved companies achieve the mandatory 25 percent Domestic Value Addition (DVA) target by the third year and 50 percent DVA target by the fifth year?

(a) the number of agricultural drones distributed to women Self-Help Groups (SHGs) under the Namo Drone Didi scheme as of January, 2026;
(b) the number of women who have completed the prescribed pilot and drone assistant training during the current financial year;
(c) the number of trained women who have obtained Directorate General of Civil Aviation (DGCA) authorised drone operation licences; and
(d) the number of women who have achieved income enhancement through drone rental services during 2024–25?

(a) the key initiatives undertaken to strengthen tourist safety and confidence, including coordination with States and local authorities;
(b) the measures taken to promote digital tourism services, unified platforms and technology-enabled visitor facilitation mechanisms;
(c) the reforms introduced to improve ease of travel and affordability for domestic and international tourists, including policy and regulatory interventions; and
(d) whether the Ministry has assessed the impact of these measures on tourist footfall, satisfaction and overall growth of tourism and if so, the details thereof?

(a) the current status of the construction of pucca houses under the Pradhan Mantri Janjati Adivasi Nyaya Maha Abhiyan (PM-JANMAN) for Particularly Vulnerable Tribal Groups (PVTGs); 
(b) the details of the approved multi-purpose centres and coordination with other welfare schemes;  
(c) the details of  the coverage of piped water supply, electrification and road connectivity in PVTG settlements; and
(d) monitoring system established to ensure effective implementation in the 18 participating States?
